WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.920
- [Narrator] With more than 65,000

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.330
square feet of space and 115 rooms,

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.130
Hearst Castle is one of America's

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.936
largest and most treasured homes.

00:00:09.936 --> 00:00:13.186
(dramatic piano music)

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.290
Hearst Castle was built by
American newspaper magnate

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.960
William Randolph Hearst in 1919

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.630
after he inherited
40,000 acres of farmland.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.970
He would go on to purchase
200,000 more acres of land,

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.140
allowing him to create
the kind of sprawling

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.453
compound rarely seen to this day.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.710
In addition to the main
house, La Casa Grande,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.620
Hearst Castle is comprised
of three guest houses,

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.423
an outdoor pool, and
numerous other amenities.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.730
One of the most recognizable
rooms in the Hearst Castle

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.880
is the 345,000 gallon indoor Roman pool.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.150
Styled after Ancient Roman baths,

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.350
the pool is decorated with eight statues

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.743
of Roman and Greek gods,
goddesses, and heroes.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.400
Hearst was known for
throwing lavish parties,

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.820
and hosting important figures
at his San Simeon home.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.600
Winston Churchill, Charlie
Chaplin, Cary Grant,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.500
Greta Garbo, and Calvin Coolidge

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.600
were some of the hundreds of house guests.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:18.150
The home was donated to the
State of California in 1958,

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.793
and welcomes more than
750,000 visitors every year.

